<title>CANADA: Hudson Bay Mining workers approve new contract.</title>
<headline>Hudson Bay Mining workers approve new contract.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unionized machinists at Hudson Bay Mining and Smelting Co's Manitoba operations have voted 78 percent in favor of the company's latest contract offer, the union said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The 208 machinists were the last group to approve a new contract. There are 1,300 unionized workers at Hudson Bay's copper and zinc operations in Flin Flon, Manitoba.</p>
<p>The new contract, which expires in December 1999, included wage and pension improvements, said Blair Sapergia, president of Local 1848 of the International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers.</p>
<p>Hudson Bay is wholly owned by Luxembourg's Minorco SA.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
